  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 21-layer alternating Ge/ZnS dielectric stack on CaF2 substrate at normal incidence. Layer 1 (Ge) thickness bounded to [452.69, 482.69] nm with target 467.69 nm. Layer 2 (ZnS) thickness bounded to [374.19, 404.19] nm with target 389.19 nm. Layers 3-21 thickness bounded to [50, 500] nm. Apply quadratic penalty weight 10x for layer 1-2 deviations beyond ±25 nm from targets. Maximize mean transmittance in passbands [4150, 4350] nm and [4550, 4750] nm. Minimize mean transmittance in stopbands [3600, 4000] nm and [4850, 5200] nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 3600-4000 nm, 4150-4350 nm, 4550-4750 nm, 4850-5200 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance in 4.15-4.35 um and 4.55-4.75 um bands; low transmittance in 3.60-4.00 um and 4.85-5.20 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance in stopbands; high reflectance in passbands. manufacturing constraints: no metal layers; maximum 24 layers; conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials.",
